592186564470 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564470 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the domain of the function $f(x)=-\\frac{1}{4}{log}_{7}⁡(2x-3)+2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564470 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1124f708-b647-5fc7-9069-27535f9fe6bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564470 #edb/ref 1074 "The domain of $y={log}_{7}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\nx>0.\n$$\n\nTo find the domain of $f(x),$ we replace $x$ with $2x-3$ in the above inequality. This gives\n\n$$\n2x-3>0.\n$$\n\nSolving this inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3 & >0 \\\\ 2x & >3 \\\\ x & >\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $y=f(x)$ is $x\\in (\\frac{3}{2},\\infty ).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564475 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564475 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81997" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564475 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564475 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the root of $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+7).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564475 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1e7e97e3-f06a-5ac7-917d-a28a5b06bd45" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564475 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+7)=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+7) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+7)} & ={e}^{0} \\\\ 2x+7 & =1 \\\\ 2x & =-6 \\\\ x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=-3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564500 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564500 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81862" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564500 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564500 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the range of the function $f(x)={log}_{2}⁡(x+4)-3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564500 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "800d4066-ddae-513f-a0b6-998ce2ab2521" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564500 #edb/ref 1074 "The range of the function $y={log}_{2}⁡(x)$ is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nHorizontal and vertical shifts and stretches do not affect the range of a logarithmic function.\n\nTherefore, the range of the given function is $f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564523 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186564398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564523 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166551" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564523 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564523 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the maximum value of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{log}⁡(3x-4)+3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564523 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cf10c890-1bed-5075-9d7f-bb216357cf94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186564523 #edb/ref 1074 "The range of the function $y=\\operatorname{log}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nHorizontal and vertical shifts and stretches do not affect the range of a logarithmic function.\n\nTherefore, the range of the given function is $f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ and the function has no maximum value." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
